=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection, unit-tested
  headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable
  state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7 AuditLogPage / ApiLogsPage / SchemaDriftPage
  do. The generated prompt's idealized "GDPRExportPage.xaml + GDPRExportPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Admin"
  is mapped onto these real conventions; the surface registers with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("GDPRExport",
  already in RouteTable.cs -> admin/gdpr-exports) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the one manifest data source is useGDPRExport (GET /admin/gdpr/exports/{id}). The view-model
  reads through an injected IGDPRExportFeed; the default EmptyGDPRExportFeed resolves the "no artifact selected" empty
  surface (the sibling-page host-injection precedent), and the generated-client-backed GDPRExportClientFeed
  (GDPRExportPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI contract client operation get_api_v1_admin_gdpr_exports_id
  with the id filling the {id} path slot (asserted in tests). No HTTP touches the view. A non-success response surfaces
  as ApiException; the view-model maps StatusCode==503 to the distinct subsystem-unavailable banner (web
  `subsystemMissing`), StatusCode==404 (and a null artifact) to the not-found banner (web `notFound`), and every other
  failure to the generic InfoBar+Retry. The lookup is a manual submit (web handleLookup: setActiveId(idInput.trim())):
  the query stays disabled until an id is submitted, so the initial state is the empty surface (web !activeId), exactly
  as the web page renders before a ?id= is supplied.
- The web page renders its data states inside the PageContainer body, so the native port reproduces them as visible
  Fluent regions per ADR-006: loading -> ProgressRing + caption; error -> TsQueryError (InfoBar-equivalent) + Retry
  (generic) or the TsAlertBanner(Danger) not-found banner (404); 503 subsystem-missing -> TsAlertBanner(Warning)
  notConfigured above the panels; empty -> TsEmptyState (download glyph); success -> the artifact section. Every web
  GlassPanel/StatCard is reproduced as a TsGlassPanel/TsStatCard Mica region, always present and toggled by the
  projected flags. Never a blank region.
- The artifact section composes the web regions from shared primitives: the status TsBadge (web Badge, STATUS_VARIANT
  map), the format/size/storage TsStatCards (web StatCard; size formatted by the 1:1 binary-unit formatBytes port), the
  artifact-details TsGlassPanel (id + TsCopyButton, user, created/completed/expires with absolute + relative time via
  DateTimeFormatting = web formatDateTime/formatRelative, SHA-256 mono + TsCopyButton), the optional export-failed
  TsAlertBanner(Danger) (web artifact.error), and the download TsGlassPanel — the Download-bundle TsButton when
  status==complete (web downloadUrl href; the conventional /api/v1/admin/gdpr/exports/{id}/download path is surfaced for
  parity/automation and the server-supplied absolute download_url is launched via Windows.System.Launcher) or the
  waiting / expired / failed caption otherwise (web downloadWait/downloadExpired/downloadFailed).
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing fields on this admin surface — an artifact-id lookup with a byte size + SHA-256 only).
  The byte size formats through the binary-unit formatBytes port (web formatBytes) and timestamps through
  DateTimeFormatting (web formatDateTime / formatRelative) at the display boundary.
- All 31 i18n keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the verbatim web key names. The 30 admin.gdprExport.* keys
  were added to Strings/{en,ar,he}/Resources.resw as translation.admin.gdprExport.* (admin.subsystem.unavailableTitle
  already present, shared with the other admin pages). The ar/he catalogs carry the English default until translated;
  the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer regardless. The four lines carrying the input-hint key
  (admin.gdprExport.idPlaceholder) carry `// parity:allow` markers (web i18n key name, not a stub placeholder).
- W1 materialization: the generated C# client (apps/windows/Generated, gitignored build artifact) was already present
  in this worktree (Generated/Api/*.cs incl. the get_api_v1_admin_gdpr_exports_id[/download] endpoints + the scaffolded
  Generated/Generated.csproj), so the whole solution builds green at baseline (0 errors). Not committed.

